tion":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.4.stable.official [4c311cbee], v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6], v4.5.dev4.official [209a446e3]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev4 - Linux Mint 22.1 (Xia) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1050 Ti (nvidia; 570.133.07) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-7300HQ CPU @ 2.50GHz (4 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe node path obtained is relative to the source object, not the target object. \nTherefore, the node cannot be found when the node path is used in the script of the target object.\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a simple scene;\n2. Attach a GDScript script to node A;\n3. Select a signal of node B and connect it to A;\n4. Open the signal connection dialog, select **Advanced**, add an extra call parameter of type `NodePath`, click **Assign...** and select a node. Click **Connect**.\n5. If the **Node** dock does not show that it is connected, repeat 4.\n6. Add the following code to the automatically generated method.\n```gdscript\nprints(has_node(extra_arg_0))\n```\n7. Run, it will output `false` when the signal is emitted.\n\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20539006/MRP.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gi